  "slug": "temporal-model-2532",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair uncertainty quantification and flux-space sampling with network-level modeling for partially observed or parameter-uncertain biological…",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is model-based inference for dynamic systems under incomplete observation or uncertain parameters. CUQDyn1 Plus addresses this through uncertainty quantification in partially observed ODE systems biology models, using jackknife+ calibration. Flux-species sampling inverts the usual workflow: it samples steady-state species and fluxes and then recovers parameters, reaching regimes that parameter sampling missed in biocircuit models. SymPerturb applies a related network-level logic to symptom networks, ranking intervention targets by a priority score, though its evidence is limited to internal simulations. What is new is the shift toward flux- and state-space exploration alongside uncertainty quantification, in place of parameter-first sampling. The three items address distinct problems rather than a single method, so the shared thread is methodological emphasis rather than common validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-28"
}
